{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "7053e3be-d47c-4971-af87-ea2ad1579f99",
    "name": "SKS Lotse Integration Tests",
    "description": "Black-box HTTP integration tests for a real, locally running backend (ENVIRONMENT unset or 'development') - not the auto-generated API reference (see sks-lotse.postman_collection.json). Run with the Collection Runner, or externally via Newman:\n\n    newman run postman/integration-tests.postman_collection.json -e postman/local.postman_environment.json\n\nor scripts/run_integration_tests.sh, which also starts nothing for you - the backend must already be running (see backend/README or `uvicorn app.main:app --reload`).\n\nFolder order matters: Auth Flow mints a token that Questions and Logout reuse, and Logout deliberately invalidates it, so Logout must run last among those three. Rate Limiting must run last overall - it deliberately exhausts the otp/request quota for this IP.\n\nSee docs/adr/0011-dev-only-otp-peek-endpoint-for-external-integration-tests.md for why this needs the /_dev-peek endpoint, and its limits (doesn't exercise the real Resend send path).\n\nNot covered: RedirectSecondaryDomainsMiddleware (backend/tests/test_canonical_domain.py). It keys off the Host header, which both Postman and Newman silently drop/override rather than send as given (a restricted header, like a browser's fetch()) - there's no way to exercise it through this tool. Verify manually instead:\n    curl -i -H 'Host: sks-lotse.com' {{baseUrl}}/health\n\nMAINTENANCE: hand-written, not generated from the OpenAPI schema like sks-lotse.postman_collection.json is - nothing regenerates or checks this collection automatically. When auth/CORS/rate-limit/questions/security-header behavior changes, update the matching request and its pm.test assertions here by hand, in the same PR as the code change, the same way backend/tests/ gets updated alongside it.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health & Docs",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "pm.test('body reports ok', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.eql({ status: 'ok' });",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('HSTS header present', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.header('Strict-Transport-Security', 'max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('X-Content-Type-Options header present', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.header('X-Content-Type-Options', 'nosniff');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('X-Frame-Options header present', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.header('X-Frame-Options', 'DENY');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Referrer-Policy header present', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.header('Referrer-Policy', 'no-referrer');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('non-API response carries no forced Cache-Control', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.not.have.header('Cache-Control');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            }
          },
          "description": "",
          "response": []
